   "title": "Hyundai Motor's HTWO teams up with Air Liquide to expand hydrogen mobility in China",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/business/companies/20261109/hyundai-motors-htwo-teams-up-with-air-liquide-to-expand-hydrogen-mobility-in-china",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Mon, 09 Nov 2026 05:57:02 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794203822.0,
   "ageDays": 0.26,
   "summary": "Hyundai Motor Group said Monday its hydrogen business brand HTWO will partner with French industrial gas company Air Liquide to expand hydrogen-powered mobility in China. HTWO Guangzhou, the Korean automotive group's first overseas hydrogen fuel-cell system manufacturing base, signed a cooperation agreement with Air Liquide China on the sidelines of the China International Import Expo 2026, which opened in Shanghai last week.",
   "summary_zh": "现代汽车集团周一表示，其氢能业务品牌HTWO将与法国工业气体公司液化空气公司合作，在中国拓展氢能交通。HTWO广州是该韩国汽车集团的首个海外氢燃料电池系统制造基地，已在2026年中国国际进口博览会期间与液化空气公司中国签署合作协议；本届博览会上周已在上海开幕。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Hyundai Motor Group said Monday its hydrogen business brand HTWO will partner with French industrial gas company Air Liquide to expand hydrogen-powered mobility in China. HTWO Guangzhou, the Korean automotive group's first overseas hydrogen fuel-cell system manufacturing base, signed a cooperation agreement with Air Liquide China on the sidelines of the China International Import Expo 2026, which opened in Shanghai last week. Under the agreement, the two companies will combine HTWO Guangzhou's hydrogen fuel-cell system technology with Air Liquide's expertise in hydrogen production, storage, transportation and infrastructure development. The partnership is aimed at accelerating the adoption of hydrogen-powered vehicles in China by integrating fuel cell technology with the hydrogen supply and refueling infrastructure",
