   "source": "sg.finance.yahoo.com",
   "published": "Sun, 08 Nov 2026 01:00:00 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794099600.0,
   "ageDays": 1.47,
   "summary": "See this month's list » The rotation follows a sharp decline in semiconductor-heavy markets after the U.S. midterm elections, with investors reassessing their exposure to companies supplying the global AI expansion. China has emerged as a potential alternative. A Hong Kong index tracking mainland Chinese companies gained 5.2% last week, its strongest performance since March 2025, as investors sought cheaper valuations and less concentrated technology exposure.",
   "summary_zh": "查看本月榜单 » 美国中期选举后，以半导体为主的市场大幅下挫，投资者重新评估其对为全球人工智能扩张提供服务的公司的风险敞口，中国则成为一个潜在替代选择。追踪中国内地企业的香港指数上周上涨5.2%，创下自2025年3月以来的最强表现，投资者寻求更低的估值以及更为分散的科技行业风险敞口。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Still guessing which stocks will beat the market? Our AI portfolio updates monthly and is outperforming the S&P 500 by 118%. See this month's list » The rotation follows a sharp decline in semiconductor-heavy markets after the U.S. midterm elections, with investors reassessing their exposure to companies supplying the global AI expansion. South Korea's Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix, alongside Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing, have faced selling pressure as doubts grow over whether AI investment will deliver sufficient profits. China has emerged as a potential alternative. A Hong Kong index tracking mainland Chinese companies gained 5.2% last week, its strongest performance since March 2025, as investors sought cheaper valuations and less concentrated technology exposure. India attracted even stronger buying. The Nifty 50 surged 8.6%, its biggest weekly advance since 2021, supported by renewed foreign interest and expectations that easing oil prices could benefit the energy-importing economy. Unsure what to buy ahead of earnings? Our AI's recent pre-earnings calls delivered gains of +77% to +118% after results dropped. See this month's earnings picks » Overseas investors purchased a net $1.9 billion of Indian equities through Wednesday, reversing earlier weakness in a market that had lagged global peers for much of the year. Investment managers are increasingly favoring domestic growth opportunities, including Indian financial companies, contract drug manufacturers and consumer-focused businesses. Vietnam is also attracting attention for its domestic growth prospects. In South Korea, investors are looking beyond major chipmakers toward cosmetics, entertainment, retail and food companies, whose revenues are less directly tied to AI infrastructure spending. Elsewhere, healthcare and consumer staples are gaining attention, alongside manufacturers that could benefit from reduced U.S. trade barriers. LG Electronics has emerged as one potential beneficiary of easing tariff pressures, given its exposure to American household appliance and television markets. Japanese and Korean automakers are also drawing renewed interest. Some investors still view the AI downturn as a buying opportunity, but the immediate shift favors diversification into businesses with different earnings drivers. Equity positioning suffered one of its sharpest weekly drops on record: DB",
